## Install

**Linux and macOS:**

```sh
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/@@REPO@@/@@BRANCH@@/install.sh | sh
```

**Windows** (PowerShell):

```powershell
irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/@@REPO@@/@@BRANCH@@/install.ps1 | iex
```

Either one downloads the latest release for your machine, checks it against the release's
checksums, and runs `@@APP@@ --install` from it. That puts the `@@APP@@` binary in `~/.local/bin`. On
Windows it adds `~\.local\bin` to your user `PATH` if it isn't there already (open a new terminal to
pick it up); on Linux and macOS, where that depends on your shell's profile, it tells you what to add
if the folder isn't on your `PATH`. `install.sh` needs `curl` or `wget`, and `unzip` (or `python3`).

Run the same command again to upgrade, or, once @@APP@@ is installed:

```sh
@@APP@@ --upgrade
```

You can also download the zip for your platform from the
[latest release](https://github.com/@@REPO@@/releases/latest) (`@@APP@@-linux-amd64.zip`,
`@@APP@@-macos-arm64.zip`, `@@APP@@-windows-amd64.zip` and so on, each for x86-64 and ARM, plus a
`SHA256SUMS`), unzip it anywhere, and run `@@APP@@ --install` from the folder it makes.
